.TH GPS-TOF-NMEA 1 "2026-11-05" "gps-tof 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gps-tof-nmea \- validate NMEA 0183 sentences and turn $GPGGA fixes into gps-tof sites
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gps-tof-nmea
[\fB\-\-yaml\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR \fIPREFIX\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads NMEA sentences from the given files (or standard input), checks every checksum
(XOR of the characters between $ and *), decodes $GPGGA (position, fix quality, satellites,
HDOP, MSL altitude H, geoid separation N, and the ellipsoidal height h = H + N) and $GPRMC
(date), and prints YAML \fBsites:\fR entries that can be pasted into a gps-tof configuration.
The generated sites use \fBdatum: msl\fR with the receiver's geoid separation, so the
datum conversion appears explicitly in the correction ledger.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-yaml
Print only the YAML site entries.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " PREFIX"
Name prefix for generated sites (default: the file name).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if all checksums are valid, 1 if any sentence fails its checksum.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    screen -L /dev/ttyUSB0 38400      # capture the TDU receiver stream to screenlog.0
    gps-tof-nmea screenlog.0 --yaml >> config/mysites.yaml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gps-tof (1),
.BR gps-tof (5)
